<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Karl Renner</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1870–1950</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Karl Renner was an Austrian Social Democratic politician who led the government of German-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> as state chancellor from 1918 to 1920. In April 1945, as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a>, he formed a provisional government that declared Austria's independence from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. He was elected the first president of the Second Republic in 1945 and held office until his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/karl-renner.jpg" alt="Karl Renner" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karl_Renner_1-E-901_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
